From article <1122@umigw.MIAMI.EDU>, by aem@mthvax.cs.miami.edu (a.e.mossberg):
> I wish Patch[1-6] would apply correctly the first time, without
> me having to repeatedly go through and manually fix things because
> some unknown person putting the patches together keeps doing things 
> like using patch to create new files instead of shar where they belong.

What version of Patch are you using?  If you have trouble using patch to
create files, you should make sure you are using the right version.  That's
not the NetHack developers fault, the current version of Patch has been
released over a year ago, and why should they be expected to worry about
being backward compatible for older versions of Patch?  It's available
via anonymous ftp from jpl-devvax.jpl.nasa.gov.

> I wish programs wouldn't depend on include files which they create themselves
> after they're compiled. The game is supposed to be the adventure, not trying
> to build the bloody thing.

Come on, if you are having trouble making the program, don't simply say
that the include file building is "stupid", but please explain exactly what
is the problem, and mail your complaints to nethack-bugs@linc.cis.upenn.edu.
How else can the developers help you??
